        '3-5', $q$Libraries on Wheels$q$, $q$(1) Not everyone can get to a library easily. (2) Some families live far from town, and others do not have a car. (3) A bookmobile solves this problem by bringing the library to them.

(4) A bookmobile is a large van or bus filled with shelves of books. (5) It follows a regular route and stops at schools, parks, and senior centers. (6) Visitors climb aboard, choose books, and check them out with a library card. (7) Many bookmobiles carry laptops and offer free internet. (8) School buses are usually painted yellow.

