   $q$Sentence 12 is a weak conclusion. Which sentence would best replace it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Next week, I am going to look for the bookmobile at my school.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"personal-ending"},{"text":"Bookmobiles have shelves, laptops, drivers, and library cards.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"list-not-conclusion"},{"text":"Some bookmobiles are much newer and shinier than others.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"new-detail-as-conclusion"},{"text":"By rolling right into neighborhoods, bookmobiles make sure distance never keeps a reader from books.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By rolling right into neighborhoods, bookmobiles make sure distance never keeps a reader from books.$q$, $q$This sentence wraps up the report by connecting back to the problem in paragraph 1, distance from a library. The list of shelves and laptops only repeats details without stating what they add up to.$q$, 'draft', 'c95712b5-1411-504b-b2ec-9755a749369f')
