insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('26e5d508-9652-5d00-ba54-e21a6c7ad793', 'wg5-informative-writing-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g5-informative-writing'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Stories in Fabric$q$, $q$(1) A quilt is a warm blanket made of three layers sewn together. (2) The top layer is often pieced from many small scraps of cloth. (3) The middle layer is soft padding, and the bottom layer is a plain backing.

(4) For hundreds of years, quilts were made mainly to keep families warm. (5) Cloth cost a lot of money, so people saved every scrap from worn shirts and dresses. (6) They cut the scraps into squares and triangles and stitched them into patterns. (7) Some patterns have names, such as Log Cabin and Flying Geese.

(8) Quilts can tell stories. (9) Some quilters sew a square for each important event in a family's life. (10) Others make memory quilts from the clothes of a loved one. (11) A quilter named Mrs. Adaeze Nwosu said, "Every square holds a memory, so the quilt becomes a family album you can wrap around yourself." (12) Neighbors sometimes work together on one big quilt, with each person adding a square.$q$, 'draft')
