insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('107cc17e-79cd-5987-9247-28719809c54a', 'wg5-informative-writing-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g5-informative-writing'), null,
        '3-5', $q$A Can's Second Life$q$, $q$(1) Every day, people drink from millions of aluminum cans. (2) Many of those cans are recycled. (3) Recycling means collecting used materials and turning them into new products.

(4) The journey of a recycled can has several steps. (5) First, cans are collected from bins and taken to a recycling center. (6) Machines sort the aluminum from glass, plastic, and paper. (7) Next, the cans are shredded into small chips and cleaned. (8) The chips are melted in a hot furnace and poured into large blocks. (9) Finally, the blocks are rolled into thin sheets that become new cans.

(10) Aluminum can be recycled again and again without wearing out. (11) A recycled can may be back on a store shelf in about two months. (12) Making a can from recycled aluminum uses much less energy than making one from new metal.$q$, 'draft')
